1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,375
This iron centre has seven neighbours: it is a pentagonal bipyramid.

2
00:00:04,675 --> 00:00:08,832
We showed it to language models as pictures and through an interactive viewer,

3
00:00:08,832 --> 00:00:11,071
and every visual run called it octahedral.

4
00:00:11,371 --> 00:00:14,058
Given the CIF text, both models got it right.

5
00:00:14,358 --> 00:00:16,714
That case is the question behind CrystalSight.

6
00:00:17,614 --> 00:00:21,220
Before a database structure is used for simulation, someone checks it.

7
00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:22,484
Are hydrogens missing?

8
00:00:22,784 --> 00:00:23,813
Is part of it disordered?

9
00:00:24,113 --> 00:00:25,490
What is the metal's coordination?

10
00:00:25,790 --> 00:00:28,249
Can it go straight into DFT or MD?

11
00:00:28,549 --> 00:00:33,997
LLM agents are increasingly asked to do this
check, and we can give them the structure as text,

12
00:00:33,997 --> 00:00:36,693
as rendered images or as an interactive viewer.

13
00:00:36,993 --> 00:00:38,500
We don't know whether those are equivalent.

14
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:43,594
CrystalSight asks the same questions about the same structures:

15
00:00:43,594 --> 00:00:49,984
67 molecular crystals from the Crystallography
Open Database and 247 questions in five families:

16
00:00:49,984 --> 00:00:55,177
hydrogen completeness, disorder, metal coordination, usability for simulation,

17
00:00:55,177 --> 00:00:56,774
and pairwise comparison.

18
00:00:57,074 --> 00:01:00,695
Gold answers are computed with MolCrysKit plus documented rules,

19
00:01:00,695 --> 00:01:04,145
and every answer is scored automatically with partial credit.

20
00:01:05,045 --> 00:01:10,805
The model sees one channel at a time: CIF text
with give-away disorder annotations stripped;

21
00:01:10,805 --> 00:01:14,875
the unstripped CIF as a leakage control; three MatterVis renders;

22
00:01:14,875 --> 00:01:19,758
or an interactive MatterVis ASCII viewer that it can rotate, zoom and relabel.

23
00:01:20,058 --> 00:01:24,578
Tool access to MolCrysKit is reported separately as a reference upper bound,

24
00:01:24,578 --> 00:01:27,255
because those tools compute the gold answers.

25
00:01:27,555 --> 00:01:32,844
Most structures are clean, so we also report
a balanced score and two trivial baselines.

26
00:01:33,744 --> 00:01:35,884
CIF text is clearly the best channel.

27
00:01:36,184 --> 00:01:44,522
DeepSeek-v4-Flash scores 0.950 mean and Gemini-2.5-Flash 0.823.

28
00:01:44,822 --> 00:01:51,450
Visual channels fall towards the baselines: Gemini with images scores 0.669,

29
00:01:51,450 --> 00:01:57,032
DeepSeek with the viewer 0.767 and Gemini with the viewer 0.481.

30
00:01:57,332 --> 00:02:00,349
Always answering "no problem" scores 0.678,

31
00:02:00,349 --> 00:02:06,524
so on the raw mean Gemini's image and viewer
runs do not beat saying everything is fine.

32
00:02:07,424 --> 00:02:08,904
With the same model,

33
00:02:08,904 --> 00:02:15,046
macro-balanced score drops by 0.24 to 0.28
between text and pictures or the viewer.

34
00:02:15,346 --> 00:02:17,549
The failures run in opposite directions.

35
00:02:17,849 --> 00:02:26,940
On disorder, DeepSeek in the viewer almost always
says "ordered": sensitivity 0.25, specificity 1.00.

36
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:35,028
Gemini in the viewer flags almost everything: sensitivity 0.94, specificity 0.27.

37
00:02:35,928 --> 00:02:42,262
Coordination from pictures reaches 0.64, against 0.91 to 1.00 from text,

38
00:02:42,262 --> 00:02:45,253
and that includes the iron centre.

39
00:02:45,553 --> 00:02:49,653
With MolCrysKit tools both models reach about 0.96.

40
00:02:49,953 --> 00:02:54,332
Stripping the CIF annotations changes the mean by minus

41
00:02:54,332 --> 00:02:57,916
0.004 for DeepSeek and plus 0.039 for Gemini,

42
00:02:57,916 --> 00:02:59,588
so the ranking holds.

43
00:03:00,488 --> 00:03:01,140
There are limits.

44
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:04,747
The gold labels depend on heuristic thresholds,

45
00:03:04,747 --> 00:03:09,462
and even with tools the models reach only 0.87 to 0.89 on disorder,

46
00:03:09,462 --> 00:03:12,136
so some of those labels are ambiguous.

47
00:03:12,436 --> 00:03:17,364
The benchmark covers 67 structures and two models, with one run each;

48
00:03:17,364 --> 00:03:20,649
the coordination family has only 11 questions.

49
00:03:20,949 --> 00:03:23,616
The renders may not show partial occupancy at all.

50
00:03:23,916 --> 00:03:28,977
Next: more structures and models with repeated runs, occupancy-aware renders,

51
00:03:28,977 --> 00:03:33,447
an opt-in local CSD task builder, expert review of ambiguous labels,

52
00:03:33,447 --> 00:03:37,193
and agents that combine viewing with text or tool checks.

53
00:03:38,093 --> 00:03:43,914
The code, tasks, ground truth and figures
are open, and a mock run needs no API key.

54
00:03:44,214 --> 00:03:46,158
Try your own model, or add a channel.

55
00:03:46,458 --> 00:03:47,356
The link is below.

